<Base titolo="Privacy policy" percorso={[{ titolo: 'Privacy policy' }]} descrizione="How the Ripetizioni di Analisi website processes personal data: which data it collects, what they are used for and what your rights are." lingua="en" seo={{ soloQuestaLingua: false }}>
  <p class="sopratitolo">Privacy</p>
  <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
  <p class="sommario">Which data the website collects, what they are used for and what your rights are. Last updated: 30 October 2026. This is a translation; the Italian version prevails.</p>

  <h2>In short</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The website collects only the data needed to run accounts, purchases and support.</li>
    <li>Your data are <strong>not sold or passed on to third parties</strong>, and are not used for advertising, newsletters or profiling.</li>
    <li>The only external services are the essential technical providers: <strong>Cloudflare</strong>, which hosts the website and the data, <strong>Paddle</strong>, which handles payments for the study material, <strong>Stripe</strong>, which handles payments for private lessons, <strong>Google</strong>, which hosts the videos of the video courses and the lesson calendar with Google Meet, and <strong>Resend</strong>, which sends the password reset emails and the study reminders. Each processes the data only to provide its own service.</li>
    <li>Your password is stored in hashed form and cannot be read by anyone, not even by the controller.</li>
    <li>You can ask at any time to see, correct or delete your data.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Data controller</h2>
  <p>Carmine Tornincasa, who can be contacted at <a href="mailto:carminetornincasa98@gmail.com">carminetornincasa98@gmail.com</a>.</p>

  <h2>Which data are processed</h2>
  <p><strong>Account.</strong> For those who create an account, the website stores the name, the email address, the password in hashed form, the unlocked subjects, the registration date and the date of the last login. It also stores the browser and system type of the connected devices (at most two), the channel of the first visit (for example Instagram or Google) and, if you state it when signing up, the courses you attended, are attending or purchased from Carmine. These data are used to run the account, to limit use to three devices, to unlock free subjects for course students and to provide support.</p>
  <p><strong>Study reminders.</strong> Account holders who have not visited the website for a few days receive an email recalling the last topic studied and the level reached, at increasingly longer intervals. To choose who receives it, the website uses the date of the last visit with the account and the last topic opened; the email is sent through Resend. Every email contains a link to stop receiving them.</p>
  <p><strong>Forgotten password.</strong> Those who request a new password enter the account email. The website sends a link valid for one hour to that address through the Resend sending service, which receives only the address and the text of the message. To prevent abuse the website counts each day's requests and deletes them after one week.</p>
  <p><strong>Purchases.</strong> Payments are handled by Paddle, acting as merchant of record. Payment data, such as the card and billing address, are collected and processed by Paddle according to its <a href="https://www.paddle.com/legal/privacy" rel="noopener">privacy policy</a> and do not pass through the website. The website receives from Paddle only the confirmation of the purchase with the account email, the subject and the amount, which are used to unlock the subject and to keep the sales record.</p>
  <p><strong>Group courses.</strong> Whoever enrols in a group course provides first and last name, email, phone number and, optionally, university, degree course, lecturer, exam date, notes and past exam papers (PDF or photos). These data are used to form the group, to create the course WhatsApp group and to build the syllabus on the exam papers. They are stored on Cloudflare's servers and only the controller can see them; the enrolment confirmation is sent through Resend.</p>
  <p><strong>Private lessons.</strong> Whoever books a lesson provides first and last name, email, phone number and, optionally, university, topics to cover and tax code for the invoice. These data are used to schedule the lesson, to contact the student and to issue the invoice. The lesson is added to the controller's Google Calendar with name, email, phone and topics; Google sends the student the invitation with the Google Meet link. Payment is handled by Stripe, which collects the card data according to its <a href="https://stripe.com/privacy" rel="noopener">privacy policy</a>: the website receives only the payment confirmation and the amount. Confirmation, rescheduling and cancellation emails are sent through Resend. To limit bookings left pending, the website keeps a non-reversible fingerprint of the network address of whoever books.</p>
  <p><strong>Invite a friend.</strong> Every account has a personal invite code. Whoever opens an invite link receives for 30 days the technical cookie <code>invito</code> with that code; if they create an account in that period, the site records which account invited them. This is used only to apply the first-purchase discount and to give the inviter a discount when the friend buys a subject; the inviter receives a notice email through Resend, without the friend's name or email. Discount codes are created on Paddle and linked to the purchase.</p>
  <p><strong>Formula sheets.</strong> Formula sheets can be read without an account; downloading the PDF requires an account, even with no purchases.</p>
  <p><strong>Browsing.</strong> The website counts page visits in aggregate form (day and section visited). To count the distinct visitors of each day it computes a non-reversible fingerprint from the date, the network address and the browser type; the fingerprint does not identify the person, and the network address is not stored. Fingerprints are deleted after 200 days.</p>
  <p><strong>Pi assistant.</strong> Those who use the assistant send their question, the text of the part of the page they are reading and, optionally, a photo of an exercise. This content is processed by Cloudflare's artificial intelligence service (Workers AI) only to generate the answer. The website does not keep conversations or photos: it only keeps the number of messages sent each day, to apply the daily limit. For those who use Pi without an account, the count uses a non-reversible fingerprint of the network address and the browser. The conversation is saved for 24 hours only in your browser and never reaches the website.</p>
  <p><strong>Exam compatibility check.</strong> The compatibility check (Italian pages only) receives the text of an exam paper (photos, a PDF turned into images in the browser, or typed text) and, optionally, the name of the university. Images are processed by Cloudflare's AI service (Workers AI) to transcribe the exercises. The site keeps, without name, email or account, the exam paper sent (page images and text), the result of the comparison, the subject and the university given, to improve the material and prepare similar exercises. Images may contain data written on the sheet (such as a name or student number): it is best to cover them before taking the photo. To apply the daily limit it counts the checks made by each account or, without an account, by a non-reversible fingerprint of the network address and browser. Recent results are saved only in your browser.</p>
  <p><strong>Video courses.</strong> The videos and PDFs of the video courses are stored in Google Drive folders. Those who purchased a video course request access to the folder with their Google account, and Carmine sees the email address used for the request. Google processes these data according to its <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">privacy policy</a>.</p>
  <p><strong>Contacts.</strong> If you write to Carmine on WhatsApp or by email, the message is used only to reply to you.</p>

  <h2>Where data are stored and how they are protected</h2>
  <p>Account and purchase data are stored on the servers of Cloudflare, which hosts the website. Communications with the website are encrypted (HTTPS), the password is stored only in hashed form, and only the controller can access student data, with a private password.</p>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>The website uses only technical cookies: <code>sessione</code> keeps you logged in, <code>dispositivo</code> recognises the device connected to the account, <code>fonte</code> remembers the channel of the first visit for 90 days, <code>invito</code> keeps the code of an opened invite link for 30 days to apply the discount. There are no profiling cookies and no third-party cookies for browsing. Some reading preferences, such as whether the contents panel is open or closed, are stored only on the device and never leave the browser. During a purchase Paddle, and during the payment of a lesson Stripe, may set the technical cookies needed for the payment.</p>

  <h2>Legal basis and retention</h2>
  <p>The processing of account, purchase and support data is based on the performance of a contract (Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR); aggregate statistics are based on the legitimate interest in running the website. Account data are kept for as long as the service is active, so that access can be restored to those who purchased a subject, or until you ask for their deletion. Data on booked lessons are kept for the period required by tax and accounting obligations.</p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>You can at any time request access to, rectification or erasure of your data by writing to the controller's address. You also have the right to lodge a complaint with the Italian Data Protection Authority (Garante per la protezione dei dati personali).</p>
</Base>
